<title>BRAZIL: Daimler-Benz Brazil strike enters 3rd day.</title>
<headline>Daimler-Benz Brazil strike enters 3rd day.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strike by thousands of workers at Daimler-Benz AG's Brazil truck plant which has halted production has entered into its third day, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Nearly 4,000 workers at the production line went on strike Tuesday demanding a profit-sharing program and a cut in daily working hours, he said.</p>
<p>The stoppage has reduced production by 140 trucks and bus chassis per day, the spokesman added.</p>
<p>In January, the company produced 2,539 vehicles in Brazil.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
